Q9: Acidic strength \(\alpha-\mathrm{I}\) effect \(
\alpha \frac{1}{+\mathrm{I}} \text { effect }
\) \(\mathrm{F}, \mathrm{Cl}\) exerts \(-\mathrm{I}\) effect, Methyl exerts \(+\mathrm{I}\) effect, \(\mathrm{C}\) is least acidic. Among \(\mathrm{A}\) and \(\mathrm{B}\); since inductive effect is distance dependent, Extent of \(-\mathrm{I}\) effect is higher in \(\mathrm{A}\) followed by \(\mathrm{B}\) even though \(\mathrm{F}\) is stronger electron withdrawing group than \(\mathrm{Cl}\). Thus, \(\mathrm{A}\) is more acidic than \(\mathrm{B}\).

